 the remote central Congo basin, far from the eastern conflict zones, and no armed group is known to hold or operate in it. Ikela town, the territory headquarters, is state-administered with the PNC as the main day-to-day security force and a FARDC presence. Rural villages of the Ikela and Mondombe secteurs have thin state presence and rely on customary authorities, but no non-state armed actor is reported to exercise control. Web research was unavailable for this run, so confidence is medium for Ikela town and low for rural villages."}}